{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~","id":180867,"title":"~ That Wacky and Weird Sidereal Charm Structure ~","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-26T09:25:56-07:00","id":180867,"title":"~ That Wacky and Weird Sidereal Charm Structure ~","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/df12d2cb097be3c598b84f08227af0a5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></b></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Bond:</b> All right Q, let show me this mission's gadget !<br /> <b>Q:</b> There has been new protocol regarding your gadget my dear. From now on you will have to pay for them. And also some gadget is randomly link with each other, which mean if you want your precious laser shooting pen, you will have to buy this loincloth that sing <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V5PLNMn3Wfg\" target=\"_blank\">Banana Party</a> whenever you approach a male target. Don't worry, it will also give you the ability to put anything into your mouth no matter how big and dirty it is.<br /> <b>Bond:</b> {\u0ca0_\u0ca0}<br /> <b>Q:</b> \u25d4\u1d17\u25d4 <hr /><br /> So I finally have the will to try and do a webcomic series, creating the group's Tank/Talky-guy/Nuker/Scout is quite easy (all are Solaroid), but I'm having trouble with the group Leader/Bard (a Bludsid), the problem that I seem to have is that Sidereal charmset kinda look like a Martial Art Style in its structure, meaning to get to an effect that I want equal to buying stuffs that I either probably won't use for a whole story or that there has been someone in the group who can already create that effect. I mean, look at the example in the comic, Avoidance Kata is a very unique and quite powerful power, but is gated by a Shadow Over Water expy and a so-so PD, or how Shun the Smiling Lady being the root charm for pretty the whole Socialize tree, or how I want to buff the group meatshield using Earth and Sky Bargain but having to slug through 4 combat-oriental charms !<br /> <br /> So yeah, does anybody else having this problem as me ? If you are a GM, will you allow me to just buy the charm that I want provide I meet the Essence/Ability requirement or do I have to follow the good book and buy stuffs that I think don't fit my character at all ?<br /> <br /> P/s: I'm having the same problem when trying to create an Infernal, which is why I'm so glad they will be an Ability-base splat in 3rd Edition, less one-charm-as-root problem (I just want Tragic Love Amusement, why do I have to learn the corpse-disposer charm !)<br /> <br /> P/s 2: I blame Glories for the constantly Poker-Face Saturn :O","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-16-2014, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T09:46:50-07:00","id":180949,"title":"","content":"Duck Fate is pretty cool cause it's omni-applicable. You can use it to dodge things that don't even make sense to be dodged like a bad performance review or the nagging of your mother or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T10:52:23-07:00","id":180982,"title":"","content":"Also Mr. Insecure will probably drop by pretty soon to offload his vitriol; the thread title is like one of his recent pet peeves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T10:56:57-07:00","id":180992,"title":"","content":"Well, it is a little wacky and weird, but that's why we all love it, right? What you see is what you get, but where the hell did you leave it when you were finished with it in your last incarnation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T18:59:04-07:00","id":181510,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not like it's a huge revelation that the Maidens are basically trolling their Chosen every hour of every day.<br /> <br /> Also, I would never have pictured Mars with a ponytail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=180982#post180982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Mr. Insecure will probably drop by pretty soon to offload his vitriol; the thread title is like one of his recent pet peeves.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I feel like I need to step up my complaining about Sidereals now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T19:37:43-07:00","id":181549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181510#post181510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I feel like I need to step up my complaining about Sidereals now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hereby appoint myself judge!<br /> <br /> Anywho, it's true that you often must pick up charms you don't entirely want, as a Sidereal. Mostly, I think, this problem isn't too large- in most trees, the bulk of charms are at least useful. Also, while it's true that Absence is a <i>boring</i> sort of charm, Duck Fate hardly qualifies. Expensive and cumbersome, sure, but it's pretty cool to have an absolutely omni-applicable perfect defense.<br /> <br /> Medicine is just sort of inexcusable as a tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T19:46:44-07:00","id":181556,"title":"","content":"Yeah, some Sidereal trees are better than others with respect to Charms being stuck in there that you might not want. Then again, that all depends on the character. Almost the entire Performance and Socialize trees fit my bluesid perfectly, for example, besides one or two Charms (Ice and Fire Binding comes to mind). That said, I have that problem with almost any Exalted tree, even Solars. That's why, right at the beginning of the Charm chapter in the 2e book it suggests STs be amiable toward designing your own Charms or altering Charm trees slightly to better suit a character. That suggestion should apply to everyone, including Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Case in point, I didn't want Absence for my bluesid, since I thought it was sorta boring and I already had Defense of Shining Joy. So I made an alternate Charm to replace it in the tree called Separation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T20:43:36-07:00","id":181601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181549#post181549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hereby appoint myself judge!<br /> <br /> Anywho, it's true that you often must pick up charms you don't entirely want, as a Sidereal. Mostly, I think, this problem isn't too large- in most trees, the bulk of charms are at least useful. Also, while it's true that Absence is a <i>boring</i> sort of charm, Duck Fate hardly qualifies. Expensive and cumbersome, sure, but it's pretty cool to have an absolutely omni-applicable perfect defense.<br /> <br /> Medicine is just sort of inexcusable as a tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Medicine is rather useful and it's pinnacle charm is probably the only must have but the ability to defer damage isn't bad. The real issue is how those charms were worded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T20:54:16-07:00","id":181604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181601#post181601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Medicine is rather useful and it's pinnacle charm is probably the only must have but the ability to defer damage isn't bad. The real issue is how those charms were worded.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the problem with Medicine was that not one charm actually helped you do Medicine type stuff. I think there may have been one 'Cure Disease' charm, which acted by killing the disease. Part of the problem was designing the Charms in link to the Astrological Houses, rather than the Abilities. Seriously, who attaches Medicine to The Corpse? Medicine should not be how to kill things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T21:17:07-07:00","id":181613,"title":"","content":"I thought Medicine in Endings made enough sense. You Ended disease, suffering, etc. It was an interesting take on it, so I thought. Sure, it's not that <i>heavily</i> related to healing people, but some Sidereal trees don't key to the Ability all that closely. See Ride, or like half the Bureaucracy Charms.<br /> <br /> 2.5e made it better, though. Peaceable Conclusion negated wound penalties, which is something Medicine could logically encompass. Terminate Illness has always been a very Medicine-eque Charm, and made better in 2.5e as it could cure magical sicknesses. Deferred Wounds could, well, defer wounds or poisons into the future, which is an amazing Medicine-eque Charm, as it allows you to get a patient to proper medical tools and/or antivenin. In many ways I think Deferred Wounds is one of the better Medicine Charms out there, as it not only keys off of your ability to use Medicine well, but is also great for engaging the characters in medicine related tasks; it doesn't just cure the thing away in one swoop, but gets the PC to seek out specialized doctors, medicine gods, tools, healing herbs and tonics and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T22:18:55-07:00","id":181669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181556#post181556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Case in point, I didn't want Absence for my bluesid, since I thought it was sorta boring and I already had Defense of Shining Joy. So I made an alternate Charm to replace it in the tree called Separation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you still have that charm lying around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T22:31:34-07:00","id":181672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181669#post181669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you still have that charm lying around?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...sion-on-themes</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I would never have pictured Mars with a ponytail. </div> </div> </div>It's just improvised on my part, since 2rd Core Mars looks too much like a man while GoD Mars has such a silly spike-bang (her being long hair like Mercury, Venus and Jupiter doesn't help).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 06-27-2014, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T23:46:13-07:00","id":181721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~#post180867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, do anybody else having this problem as me ? If you are a GM, will you allow me to just buy the charm that I want provide I meet the Essence/Ability requirement or do I have to follow the good book and buy stuffs that I think don't fit my character at all ?</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Ignore Charm Prerequisites?<br /> <br /> Why not Essence/Ability Requirements too, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T00:38:23-07:00","id":181741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~#post180867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P/s: I'm having the same problem when trying to create an Infernal, which is why I'm so glad they will be an Ability-base splat in 3rd Edition, less one-charm-as-root problem (I just want Tragic Love Amusement, why do I have to learn the corpse-disposer charm !)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this suspicion you are not going to be entirely happy.... (with regards this this issue)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T01:19:55-07:00","id":181763,"title":"","content":"I think we'll see bigger cascades that are organized a little more tightly around themes in Ex3 in place of the previous, &quot;Here are the 4 Charms your splat can learn for this Ability,&quot; model. It's hard to imagine Avoidance Kata at the base of a cascade but I can at least see it among more closely associated effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:48:18-07:00","id":181810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181763#post181763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we'll see bigger cascades that are organized a little more tightly around themes in Ex3 in place of the previous, &quot;Here are the 4 Charms your splat can learn for this Ability,&quot; model. It's hard to imagine Avoidance Kata at the base of a cascade but I can at least see it among more closely associated effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>....More closely associated than Duck Fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:26:08-07:00","id":181978,"title":"","content":"Has there been any spoiled material for the Sidereals? I think the only thing I have seen is this one playtest report which said something like 'I can totally see room for Sidereal mechanics in this game.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T20:51:37-07:00","id":182503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~?p=181978#post181978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any spoiled material for the Sidereals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing specific, though there's been a fair amount of talk about their place in the world and how they relate to Creation.<br /> <br /> <i>Which obviously means that their 3e mechanics will be completely terrible. Paradox will probably be made worse and Sidereals will naturally accrue it just because the Universe hates them so much.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Psst, Mercury, how often will you be awarding points?)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T03:34:42-07:00","id":182768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/180867-~-that-wacky-and-weird-sidereal-charm-structure-~#post180867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I finally have the will to try and do a <b><u>webcomic</u></b> series [...] I'm having trouble with the group Leader/Bard (a Bludsid), the problem that I seem to have is that Sidereal charmset [...] to get to an effect that I want equal to buying stuffs that I either probably won't use for a whole story or that there has been someone in the group who can already create that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a problem for a webcomic why?<br /> <br /> If the Sid is the leader, I assume she has more experience than the newly emerged Solariods, so why shouldn't she have whatever charms you (as you are basically the ST in this scenario) want her to have. Just give her extra bennies to represent having a decade of experience over the Solariods and play on.<br /> <br /> Or house-rule that in your webcomic the Sid charm tree is different. (The best Exalted webcomic egregiously house-ruled that you can create an Alchemical Exalt by grafting magitech parts onto mortals and had Sidereals ripping the paneling off the comic and using it to beat her enemies with - minor playing with the charm tree is small potatoes.)<br /> <br /> If I were running a mixed Exalt game, I'd basically let the Sid create their character using the rules in Lords of Creation to keep them on a par with Solariods.<br /> <br /> tl;dr<br /> <br /> Just give her the charms she's never going to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-28-2014, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":